      "description": "Watch Antwerp vs KSK Beveren highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 10, 2026. The stage was set for a compelling Jupiler Pro League encounter as Antwerp hosted KSK Beveren on August 10, 2026 . Both sides entered the pitch with clear ambitions, setting the tone for a match defined by tactical shifts and individual brilliance. Visitors Strike Early The match began with an unexpected setback for the away side when Viktor Boone was forced off with an injury after just 11 minutes, replaced by Yoni Gomis . Despite the early disruption, KSK Beveren managed to break the deadlock in the 30th minute. Christian Bruels provided a perfectly timed assist for Chris Lokesa , who clinical finish put the visitors ahead. The goalscorer was immediately shown a yellow card for his celebration. As the first half progressed, the physical nature of the game became apparent, with Sieben Dewaele also receiving a caution as Antwerp searched for a way back into the contest. Frey Masterclass Completes the Turnaround Antwerp returned for the second half with increased urgency, and their persistence finally paid off in the 63rd minute. Jules Ahoka found space to set up Michael Frey , who leveled the scores with a composed strike. The momentum shifted entirely towards the hosts, prompting a series of substitutions from both managers. The tactical gamble reached its climax in the 87th minute when Thibo Somers delivered a crucial assist for Michael Frey , who found the net for the second time to seal the comeback. Late yellow cards for Christian Bruels and Anthony Valencia added to the drama, but Antwerp held firm through seven minutes of stoppage time to secure the victory."
